# Code owners for safer-runner-action
#
# This repository is a security control. The compiled bundles in dist/ execute on every runner
# that uses the action, with sudo, before any workflow step runs, so a change merged here changes
# the security posture of every consuming pipeline.
#
# The org default repository permission is write, so every PortSwigger org member can push a
# branch here. Requiring review from these owners on main is what stops a change to the security
# posture landing without security or platform seeing it.
#
# Owners must have write access to the repository or GitHub silently ignores them. Verified for
# all six accounts below.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the catch-all comes first and the specific paths after it.

# Everything. The whole repository is the control, not one directory of it.
*                   @portswigger-josh @portswigger-mattlong @portswigger-amason @nresare @ps-pufferfish @Mo-PS

# What actually runs on a runner. dist/ is built from src/ but committed separately, so it can be
# changed without touching a single line of TypeScript.
/dist/              @portswigger-josh @portswigger-mattlong @portswigger-amason @nresare @ps-pufferfish @Mo-PS
/src/               @portswigger-josh @portswigger-mattlong @portswigger-amason @nresare @ps-pufferfish @Mo-PS

# The action contract: which entrypoints run at pre, main and post, and the inputs that select
# analyze or enforce mode.
/action.yaml        @portswigger-josh @portswigger-mattlong @portswigger-amason @nresare @ps-pufferfish @Mo-PS

# Dependencies pulled into the bundles at build time.
/package.json       @portswigger-josh @portswigger-mattlong @portswigger-amason @nresare @ps-pufferfish @Mo-PS
/package-lock.json  @portswigger-josh @portswigger-mattlong @portswigger-amason @nresare @ps-pufferfish @Mo-PS

# Workflows, and this file. Without this line a PR could rewrite its own review requirements.
/.github/           @portswigger-josh @portswigger-mattlong @portswigger-amason @nresare @ps-pufferfish @Mo-PS
